Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Voices from precomputed embeddings; load the Mimi encoder
 only when needed

An app that ships fixed voices needs only their embeddings (the Mimi
encoder's output for each clip), not the clips and not the encoder: the
encoder is what clones a voice, so leaving it out of a product is a
feature, and it saves ~40 MB of download.

- PocketTTS::add_voice(name, embedding) and the C API ptt_add_voice()
  register a voice from an in-memory embedding ([1, frames, dim] or
  [frames, dim], float32). It is then used by name like a WAV voice
  (the BOS embedding, if the bundle has one, is prepended as usual).
- mimi_encoder.onnx is loaded on first use, i.e. the first time a WAV
  voice has to be encoded, and may be absent otherwise. Asking for a WAV
  voice without it is an error that says so.
- ptt_encode_voice(encoder, audio, emb_path, threads) encodes a clip
  exactly as a WAV voice is encoded at runtime (mono, 24 kHz, at most
  30 s) and writes the .emb cache format, for making embeddings ahead of
  time. It needs only the encoder.
- The voice-conditioned KV snapshot is kept per voice (keyed by
  voice_hash) instead of only for the last voice, so switching between
  voices doesn't redo the conditioning pass each time. Voices from
  add_voice() never touch the disk caches (there is no file next to
  which to write them).
